  "_fork_note": "In fork mode the pinned manifest is written to a capstone-demo/ subdirectory so the upstream project's own manifest is left untouched. GitHub's dependency graph scans manifests anywhere in the repository, so both the real transitive dependency tree and the deliberately pinned vulnerable versions are detected.",
  "_unmapped_note": "internal-devtools and docs-site are deliberately left without a business process mapping. They exercise the unmapped-repository path, where criticality is scored as UNKNOWN at the median rather than LOW, so an unmapped asset surfaces for mapping instead of sinking down the queue.",
  "_scope_note_xz": "CVE-2024-3094 (XZ Utils) is deliberately absent. It is a compromise of a Linux system library distributed through OS package managers, not an application dependency declared in package.json, requirements.txt or pom.xml. It therefore falls outside the scope of SBOM-based application dependency analysis, and is reported as a scope limitation rather than a detection failure."
}